  "version": "1.0",
  "date": "2026-10-31",
  "description": "The GuitarML Classic Boost v2 (GuitarML/GuitarPedalPCBs at e2fa7e1, ClassicBoost_1590a/ClassicBoost_v2.kicad_sch, MIT, Keith Bloemer) as published: one 2N5088 common-emitter stage (430 kΩ / 43 kΩ base divider, 10 kΩ collector, 390 Ω emitter), a 100 kΩ volume, an LED, 9 V through a 1N5817; the jacks, the DC jack and the 3PDT bypass footswitch hang on pads – here on the hand-wired board 'wiring'. Transcribed for edakit's tests.",
  "purpose": {
   "use": "private",
   "market": "EU",
   "notes": "GuitarML publishes the boards for builders who order and build them for themselves. The transcription is a test of edakit, not a product."
  },
  "conventions": {
   "pin_reference": "'<designator>.<pin>' with the pin numbers of the parts entries – the KiCad symbols' where they agree; the 2N5458's custom symbol (1 G, 2 S, 3 D) and Device:LED (1 K, 2 A) turned into the entries' (2N5458: 1 D, 2 S, 3 G; LED: 1 A, 2 K)",
   "v": "per net: [min, max] in V over the intended operating states – 9 V from the DC jack; nets behind a coupling capacitor at ground with ±4.5 V of signal",
   "board": "main: the GuitarML PCB; wiring: the parts wired to its pads by hand (bought = true until edakit has a key for a hand-wired board)",
   "source": "GuitarML/GuitarPedalPCBs at e2fa7e1, ClassicBoost_1590a/ClassicBoost_v2.kicad_sch (checked against ClassicBoost_v2.kicad_pcb), https://github.com/GuitarML/GuitarPedalPCBs"
